IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-validity`
IMPORT `g2-conditions`
IMPORT `g2-temporary-licence`
IMPORT `g2-tests-fixtures`

-- g2-tests-temporary-licence.l4: tests of section 9.  Expected values decided from the Hebrew of s 9(a)(1) to (3) and (b) and of
-- Interpretation Law s 10(b) (dates by the Python calendar) before any module was run.  A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `Tests — s 9(a)(1) to (3): the foreign expert's conditions`

-- src:103 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} על אף האמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|בסעיפים 6}} {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 8|ו־8}}, הרשם רשאי לתת רישיון דרגה 3 זמני, למבקש ממדינת חוץ שמתקיימים לגביו התנאים המנויים להלן (בסעיף זה – מומחה זר), לתקופה שלא תעלה על שנה (בסעיף זה – רישיון זמני):
-- src:104 | {{ח:תתת|(1)}} הוא הוזמן לישראל לשם ביצוע עבודות במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר שתפוקת הקירור שלה מעל 70 קילו־ואט;
-- src:105 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} הוא מוסמך לבצע עבודות במערכות קירור או מיזוג אוויר במדינת חוץ וביצע בשש השנים שקדמו להגשת הבקשה לרישיון זמני, התקנה או תחזוקה של מערכות קירור או מיזוג אוויר דומות למערכות שלשם התקנתן או תחזוקתן הוזמן לישראל;
-- src:106 | {{ח:תתת|(3)}} הרשם הכיר בו כבעל מוניטין וכמומחה בעל שם בתחומו.
-- The qualifying expert (invited for a 100 kW system, authorised abroad, work in the six years before 1.9.2026, recognised) meets the conditions.
#ASSERT `s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` `a qualifying foreign expert` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` `a qualifying foreign expert` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(a)(3) — the Registrar recognised the expert as of repute and renowned in the field` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a)(3) — the Registrar recognised the expert as of repute and renowned in the field` FALSE
-- (1): "above 70 kilowatts": 70 is a grade 2 system (s 2: up to 70), so it does not qualify; 70.5 and 71 do.
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a)(1) — the expert was invited to work on a system above 70 kW` (`an expert qualifying in all but the capacity of the system, which is` 70)
#ASSERT `s 9(a)(1) — the expert was invited to work on a system above 70 kW` (`an expert qualifying in all but the capacity of the system, which is` 70.5)
#ASSERT `s 9(a)(1) — the expert was invited to work on a system above 70 kW` (`an expert qualifying in all but the capacity of the system, which is` 71)
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` (`an expert qualifying in all but the capacity of the system, which is` 70) TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` (`an expert qualifying in all but the capacity of the system, which is` 71) TRUE
-- The lead-in: an applicant from a foreign state.  (2): authorised abroad; similar work in the six years.
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` (`a foreign expert invited for a system of` 100 `kW, authorised being` TRUE `, from abroad being` FALSE `, with work` (LIST (`a piece of work abroad on` (YMD 2024 5 1) `, similar being` TRUE))) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` (`a foreign expert invited for a system of` 100 `kW, authorised being` FALSE `, from abroad being` TRUE `, with work` (LIST (`a piece of work abroad on` (YMD 2024 5 1) `, similar being` TRUE))) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a)(2) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` (`an expert qualifying in all but the work, which is` (LIST (`a piece of work abroad on` (YMD 2024 5 1) `, similar being` FALSE)))
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a)(2) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` (`an expert qualifying in all but the work, which is` EMPTY)

-- (2), the six preceding years (KIND B, outside Interpretation Law s 10): the application of 1.9.2026 looks back to 1.9.2020 and up to the day before it.
#ASSERT `s 9(a)(2) — the first day of the six years before the application made on` (YMD 2026 9 1) EQUALS YMD 2020 9 1
-- A 29 February application: the same calendar date six years before does not exist, and the window opens on 1 March (the lenient rebuilding rolls forward).
#ASSERT `s 9(a)(2) — the first day of the six years before the application made on` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2022 3 1
#ASSERT `s 9(a)(2) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` (`an expert qualifying in all but the work, which is` (LIST (`a piece of work abroad on` (YMD 2020 9 1) `, similar being` TRUE)))
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a)(2) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` (`an expert qualifying in all but the work, which is` (LIST (`a piece of work abroad on` (YMD 2020 8 31) `, similar being` TRUE)))
#ASSERT `s 9(a)(2) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` (`an expert qualifying in all but the work, which is` (LIST (`a piece of work abroad on` (YMD 2026 8 31) `, similar being` TRUE)))
-- Work on the application day itself is not "before" it (taken); the alternative counts it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a)(2) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` (`an expert qualifying in all but the work, which is` (LIST (`a piece of work abroad on` (YMD 2026 9 1) `, similar being` TRUE)))
#ASSERT `s 9(a)(2) (the application day counts) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` (`an expert qualifying in all but the work, which is` (LIST (`a piece of work abroad on` (YMD 2026 9 1) `, similar being` TRUE)))
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a)(2) (the application day counts) — the expert is authorised abroad and did similar work in the six preceding years` (`an expert qualifying in all but the work, which is` (LIST (`a piece of work abroad on` (YMD 2026 9 2) `, similar being` TRUE)))

-- FT1 (notwithstanding ss 6 and 8): TAKEN: s 6(a)(1) and (3) are not asked of the foreign expert; the alternative asks them.
#ASSERT `s 9(a) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` (`a foreign expert whose applicant is` (`an applicant who is adult` FALSE `, citizen` FALSE `, resident` FALSE `, with the record` `a clean record`)) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a) (also asking s 6(a)(1) and (3)) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` (`a foreign expert whose applicant is` (`an applicant who is adult` FALSE `, citizen` FALSE `, resident` FALSE `, with the record` `a clean record`)) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a) (also asking s 6(a)(1) and (3)) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` (`a foreign expert whose applicant is` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` FALSE `, resident` FALSE `, with the record` (`a record showing criminal conviction` TRUE `criminal charge pending` FALSE `and disciplinary conviction` FALSE))) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(a) (also asking s 6(a)(1) and (3)) — the applicant is a foreign expert meeting conditions (1) to (3)` (`a foreign expert whose applicant is` (`an applicant who is adult` TRUE `, citizen` FALSE `, resident` FALSE `, with the record` `a clean record`)) TRUE FALSE

§ `Tests — s 9(a): the term of a temporary licence (kind V)`

-- src:103 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} על אף האמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|בסעיפים 6}} {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 8|ו־8}}, הרשם רשאי לתת רישיון דרגה 3 זמני, למבקש ממדינת חוץ שמתקיימים לגביו התנאים המנויים להלן (בסעיף זה – מומחה זר), לתקופה שלא תעלה על שנה (בסעיף זה – רישיון זמני):
-- "for a period not exceeding one year": one year after a grant on 1.2.2026 ends on 1.2.2027 (IL s 10(b)); after 29.2.2024, on 28.2.2025.
#ASSERT `s 9(a) — the latest last day of a temporary licence granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 1
#ASSERT `s 9(a) — the latest last day of a temporary licence granted on` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `s 9(a) — the term of a temporary licence granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `and ending on` (YMD 2027 2 1) `does not exceed one year`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(a) — the term of a temporary licence granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `and ending on` (YMD 2027 2 2) `does not exceed one year`
#ASSERT `s 9(a) — the term of a temporary licence granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `and ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30) `does not exceed one year`
-- FT2, the alternative: Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied.  1.2.2027 is a Monday: with it a rest day the cap moves to Tuesday 2.2.2027.
GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`a calendar with Monday 1 February 2027` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 2 1)
GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`a calendar of no rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 9(a) (Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied) — the latest last day of a temporary licence granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, with` `a calendar with Monday 1 February 2027` EQUALS YMD 2027 2 2
#ASSERT `s 9(a) (Interpretation Law s 10(c) applied) — the latest last day of a temporary licence granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, with` `a calendar of no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2027 2 1

-- The Registrar's power to grant, exercised with #TRACE.  Conditions and fee, a term within the cap: the grant fulfils the rule;
-- a term past the cap is not an exercise of the power (the permission stands); the fee unpaid: no power arises.
#TRACE `s 9(a) — the Registrar may grant a temporary licence` (YMD 2026 2 1) `a qualifying foreign expert` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `grant a temporary grade 3 licence for a term ending on` (YMD 2027 2 1) AT 3
#TRACE `s 9(a) — the Registrar may grant a temporary licence` (YMD 2026 2 1) `a qualifying foreign expert` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `grant a temporary grade 3 licence for a term ending on` (YMD 2027 2 2) AT 3
#TRACE `s 9(a) — the Registrar may grant a temporary licence` (YMD 2026 2 1) `a qualifying foreign expert` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
#TRACE `s 9(a) — the Registrar may grant a temporary licence` (YMD 2026 2 1) `a qualifying foreign expert` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- The exported answer: the conditions of s 9(a) and the fee.
#ASSERT `the temporary licence may be granted` `a qualifying foreign expert` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the temporary licence may be granted` `a qualifying foreign expert` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the temporary licence may be granted` `a qualifying foreign expert` FALSE TRUE

§ `Tests — s 9(b): renewal for two further periods`

-- A temporary licence granted 1.2.2026 whose term the register records as ending 31.1.2027.
GIVEN renewals IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A Licence
`a temporary licence recorded to end 31.1.2027 and renewed on` renewals MEANS
    `a licence of kind` `grade 3 licence` `, temporary being` TRUE `, granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `, renewed on` renewals `, recorded to end` (JUST (YMD 2027 1 31)) `, revoked` NOTHING `, suspended from` NOTHING `, suspended until` NOTHING

-- src:107 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} הרשם רשאי לחדש את תוקפו של רישיון זמני לשתי תקופות נוספות שלא יעלו על שנה כל אחת.
-- The renewal's cap, counted from the last day of the term renewed: one year after 31.1.2027 ends on 31.1.2028.
#ASSERT `s 9(b) — the latest last day of a term renewing one that ended on` (YMD 2027 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2028 1 31
-- FT3, the alternative: counted from the day of the renewal (a renewal on 15.3.2027: 15.3.2028).
#ASSERT `s 9(b) (counted from the day of the renewal) — the latest last day of a term renewed on` (YMD 2027 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2028 3 15
-- Two further periods: none used, one used, both used; an ordinary licence has none.
#ASSERT `s 9(b) — the number of renewals still open to the temporary licence` (`a temporary licence recorded to end 31.1.2027 and renewed on` EMPTY) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 9(b) — the number of renewals still open to the temporary licence` (`a temporary licence recorded to end 31.1.2027 and renewed on` (LIST (YMD 2027 1 20))) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 9(b) — the number of renewals still open to the temporary licence` (`a temporary licence recorded to end 31.1.2027 and renewed on` (LIST (YMD 2027 1 20), (YMD 2028 1 20))) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 9(b) — the number of renewals still open to the temporary licence` (`an ordinary grade 1 licence granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1)) EQUALS 0

-- The power: not yet renewed: a renewal to the cap fulfils the rule; to a day past the cap, it is not an exercise of the power;
-- already renewed twice, or an ordinary licence, or the fee unpaid: no power.
#TRACE `s 9(b) — the Registrar may renew the temporary licence` (`a temporary licence recorded to end 31.1.2027 and renewed on` EMPTY) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `renew a temporary licence for a term ending on` (YMD 2028 1 31) AT 3
#TRACE `s 9(b) — the Registrar may renew the temporary licence` (`a temporary licence recorded to end 31.1.2027 and renewed on` EMPTY) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `renew a temporary licence for a term ending on` (YMD 2028 2 1) AT 3
#TRACE `s 9(b) — the Registrar may renew the temporary licence` (`a temporary licence recorded to end 31.1.2027 and renewed on` (LIST (YMD 2027 1 20), (YMD 2028 1 20))) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
#TRACE `s 9(b) — the Registrar may renew the temporary licence` (`an ordinary grade 1 licence granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1)) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
#TRACE `s 9(b) — the Registrar may renew the temporary licence` (`a temporary licence recorded to end 31.1.2027 and renewed on` EMPTY) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
